s or a piece of wood to do a repair on  their home  or or a gallon of milk whatever it is so  it's um  their policies to help low income and  all that are just reversed  it's all political and what what happens  is they end up hurting those they claim  to be helping the most  yeah exactly well that's exactly the  case and we're paying the price for the  blue state bad decisions that they made  in iowa we're cutting taxes we're  reducing regulations we've had our kids  in school  we are encouraging growth and  development and we're open for business  and it's just completely the contrast  i think he has forgotten that you know i  think he thinks we're just starting  covet that we're not on the end of it  the emergency is over and the amount of  money that's coming into our states is  just  unconscionable and in fact i sent back  95 million  uh they sent 95 million to the state of  iowa to help us get our kids back in the  classroom and i said our kids have been  in the classroom since august  this is ridiculous they're sitting on  700 million right now  to address testing and vaccines and to  help address covet issues and so i said  here you can take the  the 95 million back uh we don't need it  we need to do more of that  um it's it's just unconscionable the  amount of money that's going on  a lot you're trying to take  attached to dictate policy to all of you  that if you take the money you cannot  cut taxes i can't cut taxes  we're cutting taxes yeah yeah wow so  joe biden needs to stop trying to rescue  us we don't need to be rescued  we've we've said that this this money is  really a blue state bailout for the  failures that they've had in the past  what reward you get to be a governor  that actually tightened your belt  cut your budget and lived within your  means i said in my second state of the  state i'd be remiss if i didn't thank my  partner  in growing arizona's economy and that  was then california governor jerry brown  gavin newsom's even been more helpful  and think about it sean ronald reagan  said if the  if the pilgrims would have landed in  california they would have never  discovered the rest of the country  nobody leaves california because they  want to  it's becoming too painful the lack of  opportunity pushing them out  the first time in 171 years they lost  population  and it's a result of leadership policy  and lack of quality of life and economic  opportunity and you know what's even  more ironic  gavin's going to take your money checks  are going to go out to  two-thirds of the people in california  just prior to the recall i don't know  where i grew up in new york  we have different words for that um but  it's but it's from your taxpayers  you think about and you look at the tax  policies and you look at  washington when donald trump became  president  and he put his tax plan in place he got  rid of reductions or  deductions for state and local income  taxes  now personally that hurt me was it the  right thing to do  yes because red states that elect  fiscally responsible  politicians they're being punished they  didn't get the same benefit that i was  getting  now looks like joe's going to go back  and reward his blue state friends  and reinstate that deduction that's  going to hurt every one of you governor  so it it takes from our states and it  not only subsidizes bad blue state  policy it subsidizes very wealthy  taxpayers in those states and so um it's  terrible policy you know when uh  new york you know you and i have talked  about it you guys have millions of  people fewer than florida  your budget's over twice the size of the  budget in the state of florida but yet  and the infrastructure is a disaster our  infrastructure is much better we do  better in k-12  my university system is ranked number  one by u.s news and world report four  years in a row  so you know it just shows you a lot of  that money's being frittered away  but they never make tough choices when  covet hit  the legislature 